postmortems anchored to evidence, with trigger vs root cause, duration gaps and open questions.",[64,65,66,67,10],"postmortem","incident","outage","sre",{"slug":69,"kind":4,"description":70,"keywords":71},"pr","Opens a pull request with a short body that says why, following strict writing rules: no test plan, no file lists, no dashes.",[72,26,44,73],"git","writing",{"slug":75,"kind":4,"description":76,"keywords":77},"pr-address-comments","Pulls review comments on your PR, fixes what is actionable, and pushes, without ever writing to GitHub.",[26,44,78,16],"review",{"slug":80,"kind":4,"description":81,"keywords":82},"release-version-bump","Cut a release for one project in a monorepo: sync, bump only if needed, tag with the CI tag prefix, push.",[83,84,85,86,56],"release","version","tag","monorepo",{"slug":88,"kind":4,"description":89,"keywords":90},"review-pr","Reviews someone else's pull request end to end and writes the review as a local draft file, never posted.",[26,44,17,78],{"slug":92,"kind":4,"description":93,"keywords":94},"start","Pulls the default branch, cuts a named branch from your task description, and starts working on the task.",[72,95,49],"branch",{"slug":97,"kind":4,"description":98,"keywords":99},"test-feature-locally","Verify a change end to end before a PR: bring up compose, start the dev server, drive the touched flow with Playwright.",[100,101,102,103,104],"testing","playwright","docker","e2e","local",{"slug":106,"kind":107,"description":108,"keywords":109},"format-on-edit","hook","Formats and lints each file Claude writes or edits with the tools the project already has.",[34,110,111,112,113],"format","lint","prettier","eslint",{"slug":115,"kind":107,"description":116,"keywords":117},"guard","Denies merges, closes, secret reads, container teardown and shell rewrites of tracked files until you give the go.",[34,118,119,72,120],"safety","secrets","guardrails",{"slug":122,"kind":107,"description":123,"keywords":124},"pre-ship-gate","Refuses commits and PRs that mix moves with logic, add dependencies, skip tests or are too big to review.",[34,72,44,78,125],"size",{"slug":127,"kind":107,"description":128,"keywords":129},"review-chain","Blocks the PR skill until code-review, ponytail-review and comment-cleanup have run in the session.",[34,78,44,49],{"slug":131,"kind":107,"description":132,"keywords":133},"stop-check","Blocks the end of a turn while a changed JS/TS project fails its typecheck or related tests.",[34,134,135,136,137],"typecheck","tests","javascript","typescript",{"slug":139,"kind":107,"description":140,"keywords":141},"text-lint","Refuses PR, issue and commit text with dashes, test plan sections, tables, hard wraps or features framed as fixes.",[34,73,44,142,111],"commit",{"slug":144,"kind":107,"description":145,"keywords":146},"worktree-guard","Refuses edits in the main checkout while another Claude session works there, and points you to a worktree.",[34,72,50,51,147],"sessions",{"slug":149,"kind":150,"description":151,"keywords":152},"context-hud","mod","Context window and plan usage limits at a glance: footer gauges, a per-category pane, and a warning past a threshold",[153,154,155,156,157],"context","tokens","usage","limits","hud",{"slug":159,"kind":150,"description":160,"keywords":161},"context-meter","Shows context size and session cost in the status line, and warns once when the context passes a threshold",[153,154,162,163],"cost","status",{"slug":165,"kind":150,"description":166,"keywords":167},"gh-guard","Blocks Claude from posting GitHub comments or reviews as you until you give an explicit go",[26,115,16,78,118],{"slug":169,"kind":150,"description":170,"keywords":171},"read-guard","Caps unbounded Reads of large files and tells Claude how to read the rest",[172,153,154,115],"read",{"slug":174,"kind":150,"description":175,"keywords":176},"secret-redactor","Swaps secrets, emails and IPs in tool output and prompts for stable placeholders, and restores real values in tool inputs",[58,119,177,178,179],"redaction","pii","privacy",{"slug":181,"kind":150,"description":182,"keywords":183},"smart-typecheck","After a turn that edited code, runs the check script once in each package that was touched",[134,137,111,56,86]],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"item":1,"related":25},{"slug":2,"kind":3,"description":4,"keywords":5,"version":11,"html":12,"skills":13,"hooks":17,"files":18,"sources":22},"release-version-bump","skill","Cut a release for one project in a monorepo: sync, bump only if needed, tag with the CI tag prefix, push.",[6,7,8,9,10],"release","version","tag","monorepo","npm","1.0.0","\u003Ch2>What it does\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The skill cuts a release for one project in a monorepo. It syncs your release branch, reads the tag format from the project&#39;s CI workflow, bumps the version only when the current one is already tagged, then pushes the commit and the prefixed tag. Invoking it is the go: it runs the whole chain without asking.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2>When to use it\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>&quot;Release api&quot;, &quot;cut a patch for web&quot;, &quot;bump and tag&quot;.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Each project in your monorepo has its own tag prefix (\u003Ccode>api-v1.2.3\u003C/code>) that triggers its publish workflow.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Someone bumped \u003Ccode>package.json\u003C/code> by hand and forgot the tag.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>How it works\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>Greps \u003Ccode>.github/workflows/&lt;project&gt;-release.yml\u003C/code> for the \u003Ccode>tags:\u003C/code> trigger instead of guessing the prefix.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Checks \u003Ccode>git ls-remote --tags\u003C/code> for the current version. Tagged means bump, untagged means tag only, so a version is never skipped.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Bumps with \u003Ccode>npm version --no-git-tag-version\u003C/code>, stages only \u003Ccode>package.json\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>package-lock.json\u003C/code>, and defaults to patch.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Stops and asks when production runs from a maintenance branch, because a tag cut from the main line would ship unreleased work.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Configuration\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>RELEASE_BRANCH\u003C/code>: branch releases are cut from. Default \u003Ccode>main\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>RELEASE_MAINTENANCE_BRANCHES\u003C/code>: optional glob of maintenance branches production runs from, for example \u003Ccode>release/*\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Ch2>Requirements\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>git\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>node\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>npm\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n",[14],{"name":2,"description":15,"argumentHint":-1,"invocation":16},"Use when the user asks to release, ship, cut, tag, or bump a version of a project in a monorepo. The \"go to the release branch, pull, bump, push, tag, push tag\" flow.","/release-version-bump:release-version-bump",[],[19,20,21],".claude-plugin/plugin.json","README.md","skills/release-version-bump/SKILL.md",[23],{"path":21,"html":24},"\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">name\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">release-version-bump\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">description\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">Use when the user asks to release, ship, cut, tag, or bump a version of a project in a monorepo. The \"go to the release branch, pull, bump, push, tag, push tag\" flow.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">---\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"># Release Version Bump\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Overview\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Cut a new release for a single project in a monorepo: sync the release branch, then create and push a git tag using the project-specific format defined by CI. The version bump may already be done, so \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">**check before bumping**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">. If \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`package.json`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">'s current version has no tag on the remote, someone bumped it manually and only the tag is missing. Bumping again would skip a version.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Configuration\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> `RELEASE_BRANCH`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: the branch releases are cut from. Default \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`main`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">. Below, \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`&#x3C;branch>`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> means this value.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> `RELEASE_MAINTENANCE_BRANCHES`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: optional glob of maintenance branches that production runs from (for example \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`release/*`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">). Unset means production ships from \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`&#x3C;branch>`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">Read them with \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`echo \"${RELEASE_BRANCH:-main}\" \"${RELEASE_MAINTENANCE_BRANCHES:-}\"`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> before starting.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## When to Use\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> \"Bump version and tag\", \"release X\", \"cut a patch for X\", \"ship X\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> After merging a fix or feature PR that should trigger the publish workflow\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">-\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Monorepos where each project has its own tag prefix (e.g. \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`api-v1.2.3`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">## Workflow\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">1.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"> **Sync the release branch.**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> `git checkout &#x3C;branch> &#x26;&#x26; git pull`\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">2.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"> **Find the tag format.**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Grep the project's release workflow for the \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`tags:`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> trigger. Never guess.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   grep -A1 \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"tags:\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> .github/workflows/\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">project\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">-release.yml\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   Typical pattern: \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`&#x3C;project>-v[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+*`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> gives the tag \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">`&#x3C;project>-v1.2.3`\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">3.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"> **Decide: bump, or just tag?**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Read the current version and check whether its tag already exists on the remote.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```bash\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   CURRENT\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">node\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -p\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"require('./package.json').version\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)   \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># from the project dir\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   git ls-remote --tags origin \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"&#x3C;project>-v\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$CURRENT\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">   ```\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\">   -\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\"> **Tag exists**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (non-empty output): the current version is already released. \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-light-font-weight:bold;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark-font-weight:bold\">**Bump**\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-l